WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.340
What if every Elavon customer, from a corner café to a national retailer to a software partner, signed in at one place?

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.940
What if every device they touched felt like the same company?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.670
And what if our scale became their advantage?

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.967
This is Elavon One. One portal. One app. One platform.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.801
One sign-in opens the experience each customer needs.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:29.937
And as they grow, they simply gain another view. No new login. No new vendor.

00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:34.248
Small businesses want to sell, not manage software.

00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:39.708
Elavon One gives them sales, menu, staff, loyalty and gift cards in one back office,

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:43.153
with a point of sale that works right out of the box.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.349
Enterprises need control at scale.

00:00:46.349 --> 00:00:51.099
They see every region, district and store on one map, drill down in a tap,

00:00:51.099 --> 00:00:54.437
and embed Elavon payments inside their own software.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:01:00.018
Partners need speed. Resellers board merchants and track residuals.

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:05.423
Developers build once on Elavon APIs, and reach every merchant on the platform.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:08.943
And the front office goes wherever the business does.

00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:16.653
On iPhone and Android, Tap to Pay turns the phone in your pocket into a point of sale. No extra hardware.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:23.097
The Castles S1 Mini2 fits in your palm, for tap and chip at the table, or in the line.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.600
The S1F4 Pro adds a built-in printer, for full checkout, from tableside to curbside.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.790
And the 16-inch S2Pro anchors the counter as a full register.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.630
And these devices go beyond point of sale.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.985
Developer partners can install their own apps, right on the device.

00:01:44.985 --> 00:01:47.975
Tip sharing on a phone. Loyalty on a handheld.

00:01:47.975 --> 00:01:50.250
Curbside pickup. A kitchen display.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.060
These are just examples. Partners choose what to build, and where it runs.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.747
Every sale, on every device, lands in one back office.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:06.991
Competitors ask customers to stitch together separate portals, separate apps, and separate vendors.

00:02:06.991 --> 00:02:10.903
Elavon One gives them a single relationship that grows with them.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.015
For Elavon, it means one platform to build, support, and sell.

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:18.540
Internally scaled. Externally powerful.

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:22.043
One Elavon. Let's build it together.
